{#
  The activity index: a map of every located activity, and under it every activity as a table row, newest first, all types mixed. The lat/lon frontmatter is backfilled from Eventor arena positions (script: _local/generated/eventor-coords.py) and, for the rest, the Strava export.

  The table is BOTH the page's index and the map's data source: <place-map> reads the <tr data-lat data-lon> rows on idle and drops one dot per located activity above it, named and linked from the row's first <a> — ⚠ keep the activity link the first link in the row. Rows without coordinates (indoor sessions) stay listed, just unmapped. Without JS this is the complete index by design, not a degraded state — Leaflet's markers have broken keyboard and screen-reader handling upstream, so nobody is routed through the map to reach a post.

  Iterate collections.activity DIRECTLY, not through | located. `byCategory` already reverses the collection to newest-first, and `located` reverses again — the two cancelled out and the list ran oldest-first for months.

  The empty .place-map-live box is rendered here on purpose. place-map.js used to create and prepend it after idle, which shoved the whole list down on every load; its 16:9 aspect-ratio now holds the space from first paint and the JS adopts this box instead of building one.

  Sorting is <sortable-table> (webc/sortable-table.webc): data-sort is the raw value a column sorts by. data-table-priority columns drop out as the table narrows, 4 first, then 3, then 2 (table.css); each activity's page shows them all.

  No async shortcodes here, so the interlinker {% if %}-include trap doesn't apply.
#}
<place-map @place="my activities" @breakout="popout">
  {%- if collections.activity | located | length %}
    <div class="place-map-live" data-place-map-box>
      <p class="place-map-pending">Map of my activities</p>
    </div>
  {%- endif %}
  <sortable-table>
    <div class="table-wrapper" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="activities-caption" data-table-rows="link">
      <table data-place-list>
        <caption id="activities-caption">Every activity</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col" aria-sort="descending">Date</th>
            <th scope="col">Activity</th>
            <th scope="col" data-table-priority="4">Type</th>
            <th scope="col" data-numeric data-table-priority="2">Distance <small>km</small></th>
            <th scope="col" data-numeric data-table-priority="2">Time</th>
            <th scope="col" data-numeric data-table-priority="3" data-sort-first="ascending">Pace <small>min/km</small></th>
            <th scope="col" data-numeric data-table-priority="3">Heart rate <small>avg/max</small></th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {%- for post in collections.activity %}
            {%- set d = post.data %}
            {%- set day = post.date | formatDate('D MMM YYYY') %}
            {%- set p = d.activityType | pace(d.distanceKm, d.duration) %}
            {#- data-date is the marker popup's first line; it matches the visible date. -#}
            <tr{% if d.lat and d.lon %} data-lat="{{ d.lat }}" data-lon="{{ d.lon }}" data-date="{{ day }}"{% endif %}>
              <td data-sort="{{ post.date.getTime() }}"><time datetime="{{ post.date | toIsoString }}">{{ day }}</time></td>
              <th scope="row"><a href="{{ post.url }}"{% if d.titleLang %} lang="{{ d.titleLang }}"{% endif %}>{{ d.title }}</a></th>
              <td data-table-priority="4">{{ d.activityType | capitalize }}</td>
              <td data-numeric data-table-priority="2" data-sort="{{ d.distanceKm }}">{{ d.distanceKm.toFixed(1) if d.distanceKm }}</td>
              <td data-numeric data-table-priority="2" data-sort="{{ d.duration }}">{{ d.duration | itunesDuration }}</td>
              <td data-numeric data-table-priority="3" data-sort="{{ (d.duration / d.distanceKm) | round if p }}">{{ p }}</td>
              <td data-numeric data-table-priority="3" data-sort="{{ d.hrAvg }}">{% if d.hrAvg %}{{ d.hrAvg }}/{{ d.hrMax or '–' }}{% endif %}</td>
            </tr>
          {%- endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </sortable-table>
</place-map>
